"""AQS-DUTY-051. EW_1 to EW_9 cell sizing from the graph harvest edges.
Basis: IA-EW-MET-n is a copper-equivalent sheet rate (AQS-ASSAY-001 section 4), so the bounding current is
I = m / (M_Cu/(2F) * 86400) / FE. Element current from the S08 deposits (AQS-ASSAY-001 section 5) is shown for
comparison. Study values are labeled and are in AQS-REG-002."""
import json, math, sys, os
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))
from flow_graph.param import drivers as DR
from flow_graph.param.constants import M as _M
from flow_graph.param.sizing import electrochem
_d=DR.load(); MCU=_M['Cu']
g=json.load(open('flow_graph/plant_flow_graph.json')); R={e['stream_id']:e['rate']['value'] for e in g['edges']}
EL={1:('Au',196.97,3),2:('Ag',107.87,1),3:('Cu',63.546,2),4:('Pb',207.2,2),5:('Sn',118.71,2),
    6:('Ni',58.693,2),7:('Fe',55.845,2),8:('Cd',112.41,2),9:('Zn',65.38,2)}
DEP={int(k):x for k,x in DR.val(_d,'DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_s08_deposits_kg_d').items()}   # AQS-ASSAY-001 section 5
FE=DR.val(_d,'ew_current_efficiency_design')   # drivers.json (needs_verification; published 0.85-0.92, SCHLESINGER2011)
J=DR.val(_d,'ew_current_density_A_m2')        # SCHLESINGER2011
PH=DR.val(_d,'DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_plate_height_m')    # A-M-040 (AQS-EW-MOD-001)
PW=DR.val(_d,'DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_plate_width_m')     # A-M-040 (AQS-EW-MOD-001)
AP=2*PH*PW       # both faces
PITCH=DR.val(_d,'DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_cathode_pitch_m')  # A-M-038 (50 mm cathode-anode)
V=DR.val(_d,'ew_cell_voltage_V')                # drivers.json (needs_verification)
WALL=DR.val(_d,'DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_tank_wall_m')       # AQS-DUTY-051 Rev A
END=DR.val(_d,'DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_tank_end_margin_m'); SIDE=DR.val(_d,'DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_tank_side_margin_m')
SUMP=DR.val(_d,'DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_tank_sump_m'); TOP=DR.val(_d,'DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_tank_cover_m'); FB=DR.val(_d,'DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_tank_freeboard_m')   # A-M-038 allowances
rows=[]
for n in range(1,10):
    m=R[f'IA-EW-MET-{n}']+(R['IA-EW-SHEET'] if n==9 else 0); el,M,z=EL[n]; dep=DEP[n]   # EW_9 also books IA-EW-SHEET
    I=electrochem.faraday_current_A(m,MCU,2,FE)
    Iel=electrochem.faraday_current_A(dep,M,z,1.0)
    Nc=electrochem.cathode_count(I,J,AP); j=I/(Nc*AP)
    Li=Nc*PITCH+2*END; Wi=PW+2*SIDE; Hi=SUMP+PH+TOP+FB
    Lo,Wo,Ho=[round((x+2*WALL)*1000) for x in (Li,Wi)]+[round((Hi+WALL)*1000)]
    Vl=Li*Wi*(SUMP+PH+TOP); Q=R[[e['stream_id'] for e in g['edges'] if e['to_unit_id']==f'EW_{n}' and e['stream_id'].startswith('IA-EW')][0]]/DR.val(_d,'DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_liquor_rho_kg_m3')   # A-M-029
    rows.append(dict(cell=f'EW_{n}',metal=el,edge_kg_d=m,I_A=I,I_elem_A=Iel,cathodes=Nc,anodes=Nc+1,j_A_m2=j,
        size_mm=[Lo,Wo,Ho],V_liq_m3=Vl,tau_min=Vl/Q*1440,P_kW=electrochem.dc_power_kW(I,V)))
tot=dict(I_A=sum(r['I_A'] for r in rows),I_elem_A=sum(r['I_elem_A'] for r in rows),P_kW=sum(r['P_kW'] for r in rows))
MD=os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)),'sizing','EW_CELLS.md')
def write_md():
    """AQS-DUTY-051: this duty sheet is a generator output (X-GOV-06 register clears at the commit that carries it)."""
    Ls=[r['size_mm'][0] for r in rows]
    X=['# EW_1 to EW_9 cell sizing','', 'Document number: AQS-DUTY-051', 'Revision: D', 'Date: 2026-10-29',
       'Generated by `docs-authority/_ew_sizing.py` from the plant graph and `flow_graph/param/drivers.json` (AQS-PAR-001). Do not edit by hand; change the generator or its inputs and run `python3 -m flow_graph.param.regen`.',
       f"Authority: graph Rev {g['revision']}; unit tasks MET-EW_n-02 of AQS-PLAN-007; study values in AQS-REG-002 (A-M-036 to A-M-040). Study. Not a PE stamp.", '',
       '| Rev | Description | Date |', '| --- | --- | --- |',
       '| A | First issue: current, electrodes, tank size, holdup and DC power of each cell | 2026-10-15 |',
       '| B | Acid-loop decision of task X-PAR: current efficiency and cell voltage set on the chloride electrowinning basis | 2026-10-15 |',
       '| C | Written by the script from the graph; currents and tank sizes unchanged, residence times follow the cascade transit rates | 2026-10-18 |',
       '| D | Purpose and scope added; the basis written as sentences with the driver values in place of fixed figures; findings computed from the results where they quote them | 2026-10-29 |', '',
       '## 1. Purpose and scope', '',
       'This page sizes the nine electrowinning (EW) cells `EW_1` to `EW_9` of the cascade, each of which plates one metal from the leach liquor. For each cell it gives the current, the number of electrodes, the tank size, the liquor holdup, the residence time and the direct-current (DC) power.', '',
       '## 2. Basis', '',
       f'The harvest stream IA-EW-MET-n of each cell is a copper-equivalent sheet rate that bounds the mass of the element (AQS-ASSAY-001 section 4); EW_9 also takes the sheet stream IA-EW-SHEET. The bounding current is I = m / (M_Cu / 2F × 86 400) / CE, with a current efficiency CE of {FE} (driver `ew_current_efficiency_design`; [USBM_CL_EW] gives 0.85 to 0.90 for chloride electrowinning; A-M-036). '
       "For comparison, the element current is computed from the S08 deposits of AQS-ASSAY-001 section 5 with the valence of each metal.",
       f'The cathode current density is {J:g} A/m² (AQS-EW-MOD-001). Each plate is immersed over {PW:g} m of width and {PH:g} m of depth, so its two faces give {AP:.3f} m². The cathode pitch is {PITCH*1000:.0f} mm with an anode between each pair of cathodes, and there is one more anode than cathodes.',
       f'The inside length of a tank is the number of cathodes times the pitch plus {END*1000:.0f} mm at each end; the inside width is the plate width plus {SIDE*1000:.0f} mm at each side; the inside depth is a {SUMP*1000:.0f} mm sump, the plate, a {TOP*1000:.0f} mm cover and {FB*1000:.0f} mm of freeboard. The wall is {WALL*1000:.0f} mm, and the liquor density is {DR.val(_d,"DIGESTER.ew-cascade-train.ew_liquor_rho_kg_m3"):g} kg/m³ (AQS-DUTY-050).',
       f'The cell voltage is {V:g} V (driver `ew_cell_voltage_V`), from the 2.1 kWh per kilogram of copper that [USBM_CL_EW] gives for cupric chloride (A-M-039).', '',
       '## 3. Results', '', 'Table 3.1 gives the size of each cell.', '', 'Table 3.1. Electrowinning cells', '',
       '| Cell | Metal | Edge kg/d | I bounding, A | I element, A | Cathodes / anodes | j, A/m² | Tank L × W × H, mm | Liquor m³ | Residence, min | DC kW |',
       '| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |']
    for r in rows:
        X.append(f"| {r['cell']} | {r['metal']} | {r['edge_kg_d']:.2f} | {round(r['I_A'])} | {r['I_elem_A']:.1f} | {r['cathodes']} / {r['anodes']} | {round(r['j_A_m2'])} |"
                 f" {r['size_mm'][0]} × {r['size_mm'][1]} × {r['size_mm'][2]} | {r['V_liq_m3']:.3f} | {round(r['tau_min'])} | {r['P_kW']:.2f} |")
    X += [f"| Total | | | {round(tot['I_A'])} | {round(tot['I_elem_A'])} | | | | | | {tot['P_kW']:.2f} |", '',
       '## 4. Findings', '',
       f"1. The envelope `size_mm` on each EW node is the cathode plate, not the cell. The tank sizes of Table 3.1, from {min(Ls)} mm to {max(Ls)} mm long, are written to `params.sizing.size_mm`; the graph `size_mm` and the placement rows are not changed here. The cells were placed in the aisle by `flow_graph/place_ew_aisle.py` (X-RSZ-03).",
       f"2. The bounding DC load at the electrodes is {tot['P_kW']:.1f} kW at {round(tot['I_A'])} A. The graph streams IA-DC-EW_n carry the cell power plus the bus voltage drop, as written by `flow_graph/param/write_graph.py` (AQS-ELEC-004).",
       f"3. The element current is {round(tot['I_elem_A'])} A, {tot['I_A']/tot['I_elem_A']:.1f} times lower. The bounding case sets the hardware; the element case is the expected operating point at the reference feed.",
       '4. Side-reaction H₂ on EW_1, EW_2, EW_4 and EW_9 (graph H₂ edges) would add Faradaic current not counted here. It is held with the AQS-DUTY-016 H₂/Cl₂ discrepancy (EDGE_RATING_DUTY) and needs an owner rate decision.',
       '5. The 316L frame in AQS-EW-MOD-001 is a wetted metal that is not an electrode, and it is withdrawn under rule M3 of AQS-STD-002; the racks are CPVC or PVC-U. The electrodes, first 316L cathodes and PbO₂ anodes, were reopened for chloride service with chlorine at the anode (X-MAT-18) and are now titanium cathodes and mixed-metal-oxide anodes (AQS-STD-002 section 9).']
    open(MD,'w').write('\n'.join(X)+'\n')
if __name__=='__main__':
    write_md()
    print(json.dumps(dict(rows=rows,total=tot),indent=1))
